    <title>open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib - Releases - 2026-11-05</title>
    <id>https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib#2026-11-05</id>
    <link href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib" />
    <updated>2026-11-06T00:06:29Z</updated>
    <content type="html">
                &lt;div&gt;
                    
                        &lt;article&gt;
                            &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/releases/tag/Instrumentation.Http-1.20.2"&gt;Instrumentation.Http-1.20.2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
                            &lt;div&gt;
                                &lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NuGet: &lt;a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.Http/1.20.2" rel="nofollow"&gt;OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.Http v1.20.2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Updated Semantic Conventions version to &lt;code&gt;1.45.0&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
(&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5833" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5833/hovercard"&gt;#5833&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fixed an issue on .NET Framework where an asynchronous &lt;code&gt;HttpWebRequest&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
(including &lt;code&gt;HttpClient&lt;/code&gt;) that waited for a free connection could be sent with&lt;br&gt;
the trace context and baggage of another request.&lt;br&gt;
(&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5873" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5873/hovercard"&gt;#5873&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See &lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/blob/Instrumentation.Http-1.20.2/src/OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.Http/CHANGELOG.md"&gt;CHANGELOG&lt;/a&gt; for details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
                            &lt;/div&gt;
                        &lt;/article&gt;
                    
                        &lt;article&gt;
                            &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/releases/tag/Instrumentation.Hangfire-1.20.2-beta.1"&gt;Instrumentation.Hangfire-1.20.2-beta.1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
                            &lt;div&gt;
                                &lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NuGet: &lt;a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.Hangfire/1.20.2-beta.1" rel="nofollow"&gt;OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.Hangfire v1.20.2-beta.1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fixed failed jobs exporting the exception message as the span status description.&lt;br&gt;
The message is now only recorded when &lt;code&gt;RecordException&lt;/code&gt; is enabled.&lt;br&gt;
(&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5884" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5884/hovercard"&gt;#5884&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fixed baggage from a job being visible to work started by other jobs&lt;br&gt;
performed on the same worker.&lt;br&gt;
(&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5886" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5886/hovercard"&gt;#5886&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Added &lt;code&gt;EnrichWithBackgroundJob&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;CustomStateMappings&lt;/code&gt; to&lt;br&gt;
&lt;code&gt;HangfireMetricsInstrumentationOptions&lt;/code&gt;. Use them to add custom attributes to&lt;br&gt;
the metrics and to count jobs in custom Hangfire states.&lt;br&gt;
(&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5810" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5810/hovercard"&gt;#5810&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fixed &lt;code&gt;workflow.execution.duration&lt;/code&gt; for the &lt;code&gt;executing&lt;/code&gt; state. It included the&lt;br&gt;
time of other measurements of this instrumentation, for example the database&lt;br&gt;
query that &lt;code&gt;RecordQueueLatency&lt;/code&gt; adds.&lt;br&gt;
(&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5810" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5810/hovercard"&gt;#5810&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See &lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/blob/Instrumentation.Hangfire-1.20.2-beta.1/src/OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.Hangfire/CHANGELOG.md"&gt;CHANGELOG&lt;/a&gt; for details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
                            &lt;/div&gt;
                        &lt;/article&gt;
                    
                        &lt;article&gt;
                            &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/releases/tag/OpAmp.Client-0.10.0-alpha.1"&gt;OpAmp.Client-0.10.0-alpha.1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
                            &lt;div&gt;
                                &lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NuGet: &lt;a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/OpenTelemetry.OpAmp.Client/0.10.0-alpha.1" rel="nofollow"&gt;OpenTelemetry.OpAmp.Client v0.10.0-alpha.1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fixed &lt;code&gt;OpAmpClient.FlushAsync()&lt;/code&gt; potentially waiting indefinitely when new&lt;br&gt;
messages kept being queued. Messages queued after a flush starts no longer&lt;br&gt;
delay its completion.&lt;br&gt;
(&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5882" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5882/hovercard"&gt;#5882&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fixed the pending message byte limit not counting state reports queued together&lt;br&gt;
with custom messages, which allowed pending frames to retain more memory than&lt;br&gt;
the configured limit.&lt;br&gt;
(&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5881" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5881/hovercard"&gt;#5881&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Breaking change:&lt;/strong&gt; Renamed &lt;code&gt;OpAmpClientSettings.MaxPendingCustomMessageBytes&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
to &lt;code&gt;MaxPendingMessageBytes&lt;/code&gt; to reflect that the limit also counts state reports&lt;br&gt;
queued with custom messages.&lt;br&gt;
(&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5881" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5881/hovercard"&gt;#5881&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fix WebSocket transport startup blocking when the server sends messages&lt;br&gt;
immediately after the handshake.&lt;br&gt;
(&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5883" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5883/hovercard"&gt;#5883&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Breaking Change&lt;/strong&gt;: The default HTTP client and the default WebSocket&lt;br&gt;
client no longer follow HTTP redirects. A redirect response now fails the&lt;br&gt;
request or connection instead of being followed. To restore redirects, set&lt;br&gt;
the new &lt;code&gt;OpAmpClientSettings.AllowRedirects&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;true&lt;/code&gt;; it does not apply to&lt;br&gt;
clients returned by &lt;code&gt;HttpClientFactory&lt;/code&gt; or &lt;code&gt;ClientWebSocketFactory&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
WebSocket redirects cannot be disabled on .NET Framework and&lt;br&gt;
.NET Standard 2.0 targets.&lt;br&gt;
(&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5885" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5885/hovercard"&gt;#5885&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See &lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/blob/OpAmp.Client-0.10.0-alpha.1/src/OpenTelemetry.OpAmp.Client/CHANGELOG.md"&gt;CHANGELOG&lt;/a&gt; for details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
                            &lt;/div&gt;
                        &lt;/article&gt;
                    
                        &lt;article&gt;
                            &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/releases/tag/Resources.Azure-1.20.2-beta.1"&gt;Resources.Azure-1.20.2-beta.1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
                            &lt;div&gt;
                                &lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NuGet: &lt;a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/OpenTelemetry.Resources.Azure/1.20.2-beta.1" rel="nofollow"&gt;OpenTelemetry.Resources.Azure v1.20.2-beta.1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Updated Semantic Conventions version to &lt;code&gt;1.45.0&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
(&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5833" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5833/hovercard"&gt;#5833&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Azure VM resource detector no longer follows HTTP redirects returned by&lt;br&gt;
the Azure Instance Metadata Service endpoint. A redirect response is now&lt;br&gt;
treated as a failed detection.&lt;br&gt;
(&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5843" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5843/hovercard"&gt;#5843&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See &lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/blob/Resources.Azure-1.20.2-beta.1/src/OpenTelemetry.Resources.Azure/CHANGELOG.md"&gt;CHANGELOG&lt;/a&gt; for details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
                            &lt;/div&gt;
                        &lt;/article&gt;
                    
                        &lt;article&gt;
                            &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/releases/tag/Sampler.AWS-0.1.0-alpha.18"&gt;Sampler.AWS-0.1.0-alpha.18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
                            &lt;div&gt;
                                &lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NuGet: &lt;a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/OpenTelemetry.Sampler.AWS/0.1.0-alpha.18" rel="nofollow"&gt;OpenTelemetry.Sampler.AWS v0.1.0-alpha.18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fixed the attributes of a sampling rule being matched incorrectly when a span&lt;br&gt;
has more than one tag with the same key.&lt;br&gt;
(&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5824" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5824/hovercard"&gt;#5824&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The sampling endpoint client no longer follows HTTP redirects or retains&lt;br&gt;
cookies. A redirect response is now treated as a failed poll, so deployments&lt;br&gt;
that rely on a redirect in front of the sampling endpoint must configure the&lt;br&gt;
final URL via &lt;code&gt;SetEndpoint&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
(&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5856" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5856/hovercard"&gt;#5856&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See &lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/blob/Sampler.AWS-0.1.0-alpha.18/src/OpenTelemetry.Sampler.AWS/CHANGELOG.md"&gt;CHANGELOG&lt;/a&gt; for details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
                            &lt;/div&gt;
                        &lt;/article&gt;
                    
                        &lt;article&gt;
                            &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/releases/tag/Resources.AWS-1.20.2"&gt;Resources.AWS-1.20.2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
                            &lt;div&gt;
                                &lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NuGet: &lt;a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/OpenTelemetry.Resources.AWS/1.20.2" rel="nofollow"&gt;OpenTelemetry.Resources.AWS v1.20.2&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;AWSEC2Detector&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;AWSECSDetector&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;AWSEKSDetector&lt;/code&gt; no longer follow HTTP&lt;br&gt;
redirects when requesting metadata. A redirect response is now treated as a&lt;br&gt;
failed request.&lt;br&gt;
(&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5878" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5878/hovercard"&gt;#5878&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See &lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/blob/Resources.AWS-1.20.2/src/OpenTelemetry.Resources.AWS/CHANGELOG.md"&gt;CHANGELOG&lt;/a&gt; for details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
                            &lt;/div&gt;
                        &lt;/article&gt;
                    
                        &lt;article&gt;
                            &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/releases/tag/Instrumentation.Owin-1.20.2-beta.1"&gt;Instrumentation.Owin-1.20.2-beta.1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
                            &lt;div&gt;
                                &lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NuGet: &lt;a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.Owin/1.20.2-beta.1" rel="nofollow"&gt;OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.Owin v1.20.2-beta.1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Updated Semantic Conventions version to &lt;code&gt;1.45.0&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
(&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5833" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5833/hovercard"&gt;#5833&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Breaking Change&lt;/strong&gt;: The &lt;code&gt;http.server.request.duration&lt;/code&gt; metric no longer&lt;br&gt;
includes the &lt;code&gt;http.request.method_original&lt;/code&gt; tag, and records only the&lt;br&gt;
normalized &lt;code&gt;http.request.method&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
(&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5880" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5880/hovercard"&gt;#5880&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See &lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/blob/Instrumentation.Owin-1.20.2-beta.1/src/OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.Owin/CHANGELOG.md"&gt;CHANGELOG&lt;/a&gt; for details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
                            &lt;/div&gt;
                        &lt;/article&gt;
                    
                        &lt;article&gt;
                            &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/releases/tag/Instrumentation.ConfluentKafka-0.5.0-alpha.1"&gt;Instrumentation.ConfluentKafka-0.5.0-alpha.1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
                            &lt;div&gt;
                                &lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NuGet: &lt;a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.ConfluentKafka/0.5.0-alpha.1" rel="nofollow"&gt;OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.ConfluentKafka v0.5.0-alpha.1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Breaking change&lt;/strong&gt;: Updated the traces and metrics emitted by the Kafka&lt;br&gt;
producer and consumer to follow the&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/semantic-conventions/tree/v1.45.0/docs/messaging"&gt;v1.45.0 messaging semantic conventions&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
The following attributes were renamed:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;messaging.system.name&lt;/code&gt; (replacing &lt;code&gt;messaging.system&lt;/code&gt;), on both spans and&lt;br&gt;
metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;kafka.offset&lt;/code&gt; (replacing &lt;code&gt;messaging.kafka.offset&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;kafka.message.key&lt;/code&gt; (replacing &lt;code&gt;messaging.kafka.message.key&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;kafka.message.tombstone&lt;/code&gt; (replacing &lt;code&gt;messaging.kafka.message.tombstone&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;kafka.cluster.id&lt;/code&gt; (replacing &lt;code&gt;messaging.kafka.cluster.id&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;(&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5831" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5831/hovercard"&gt;#5831&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See &lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/blob/Instrumentation.ConfluentKafka-0.5.0-alpha.1/src/OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.ConfluentKafka/CHANGELOG.md"&gt;CHANGELOG&lt;/a&gt; for details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
                            &lt;/div&gt;
                        &lt;/article&gt;
                    
                        &lt;article&gt;
                            &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/releases/tag/Instrumentation.GrpcCore-1.0.0-beta.19"&gt;Instrumentation.GrpcCore-1.0.0-beta.19&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
                            &lt;div&gt;
                                &lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NuGet: &lt;a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.GrpcCore/1.0.0-beta.19" rel="nofollow"&gt;OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.GrpcCore v1.0.0-beta.19&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fixed unbounded memory growth on streaming calls when &lt;code&gt;RecordMessageEvents&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
is enabled. At most 128 message events are now recorded per call.&lt;br&gt;
(&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5879" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5879/hovercard"&gt;#5879&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fixed &lt;code&gt;ServerTracingInterceptor&lt;/code&gt; applying the baggage received with one RPC&lt;br&gt;
to other RPCs.&lt;br&gt;
(&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5874" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5874/hovercard"&gt;#5874&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See &lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/blob/Instrumentation.GrpcCore-1.0.0-beta.19/src/OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.GrpcCore/CHANGELOG.md"&gt;CHANGELOG&lt;/a&gt; for details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
                            &lt;/div&gt;
                        &lt;/article&gt;
                    
                        &lt;article&gt;
                            &lt;h2&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/releases/tag/Instrumentation.AspNet-1.20.3"&gt;Instrumentation.AspNet-1.20.3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
                            &lt;div&gt;
                                &lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NuGet: &lt;a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.AspNet/1.20.3" rel="nofollow"&gt;OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.AspNet v1.20.3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Updated Semantic Conventions version to &lt;code&gt;1.45.0&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;br&gt;
(&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5833" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5833/hovercard"&gt;#5833&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fixed &lt;code&gt;http.route&lt;/code&gt; and the span name containing the &lt;code&gt;controller&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;action&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;
values from the request URL for conventional MVC and WebAPI routes. The names&lt;br&gt;
are now only used once a request for them has completed successfully, otherwise&lt;br&gt;
the &lt;code&gt;{controller}&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;{action}&lt;/code&gt; tokens of the route template are reported.&lt;br&gt;
(&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5858" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5858/hovercard"&gt;#5858&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See &lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/blob/Instrumentation.AspNet-1.20.3/src/OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.AspNet/CHANGELOG.md"&gt;CHANGELOG&lt;/a&gt; for details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;NuGet: &lt;a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.AspNet.TelemetryHttpModule/1.20.3" rel="nofollow"&gt;OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.AspNet.TelemetryHttpModule v1.20.3&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fixed baggage and an unstopped &lt;code&gt;Activity&lt;/code&gt; being left behind when an&lt;br&gt;
&lt;code&gt;EndRequest&lt;/code&gt; handler that runs after &lt;code&gt;TelemetryHttpModule&lt;/code&gt; throws.&lt;br&gt;
(&lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5868" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/pull/5868/hovercard"&gt;#5868&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;See &lt;a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-dotnet-contrib/blob/Instrumentation.AspNet-1.20.3/src/OpenTelemetry.Instrumentation.AspNet.TelemetryHttpModule/CHANGELOG.md"&gt;CHANGELOG&lt;/a&gt; for details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
                            &lt;/div&gt;
                        &lt;/article&gt;
                    
                &lt;/div&gt;
